#: templates/views/pages/team.htm:22
#| msgid ""
#| "ManuSpectrum archives, standardises and makes searchable the physicochemical"
#| " analysis of manuscripts and written heritage, so that reliable, "
#| "interoperable data can be reused by people who did not run the measurements."
msgid ""
"ManuSpectrum archives, standardises and makes searchable the physicochemical"
" analysis of written cultural heritage — manuscripts, printed books, "
"inscriptions and more — so that reliable, interoperable data can be reused "
"by people who did not run the measurements."
msgstr ""
"ManuSpectrum archives, standardises and makes searchable the physicochemical"
" analysis of written cultural heritage — manuscripts, printed books, "
"inscriptions and more — so that reliable, interoperable data can be reused "
"by people who did not run the measurements."

#: templates/views/pages/team.htm:29
msgid ""
"It is developed within Cluster 2 — “Consideration and searchability of "
"materials-analysis data” — of the ANR Biblissima+ programme, at the Centre "
"de Recherche sur la Conservation (CRC), in partnership with Huma-Num."
msgstr ""
"It is developed within Cluster 2 — “Consideration and searchability of "
"materials-analysis data” — of the ANR Biblissima+ programme, at the Centre "
"de Recherche sur la Conservation (CRC), in partnership with Huma-Num."

#: templates/views/pages/team.htm:36
msgid ""
"Built on Arches, it places the material component at the pivot between the "
"object, its context, the analyses and their interpretations, using shared "
"ontologies (CIDOC-CRM, CRMsci) and reference thesauri to keep heterogeneous "
"documents comparable and interoperable with the Biblissima portal."
msgstr ""
"Built on Arches, it places the material component at the pivot between the "
"object, its context, the analyses and their interpretations, using shared "
"ontologies (CIDOC-CRM, CRMsci) and reference thesauri to keep heterogeneous "
"documents comparable and interoperable with the Biblissima portal."

#: templates/views/pages/team.htm:46
